WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.212
(club music)

00:00:01.212 --> 00:00:02.687
- [Dren] It’s something that

00:00:02.687 --> 00:00:04.178
you feel a connection
with people automatically.

00:00:04.178 --> 00:00:07.099
- [Angel] I don't think
there's a better feeling.

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:09.649
You can move the night with the music

00:00:09.649 --> 00:00:12.903
and the energy of the
people can also move me.

00:00:12.903 --> 00:00:15.608
It just really feels fulfilling.

00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:18.025
(club music)

00:00:26.937 --> 00:00:29.696
- Hi, I'm Angel.
- I'm Dren.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.398
- We're twin DJs and producers.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:35.589
- [Dren] What makes a good
DJ is being observant.

00:00:35.589 --> 00:00:37.416
If I play one track and I'm just like

00:00:37.416 --> 00:00:39.273
everybody really responded to that,

00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:41.122
it's knowing in your
head in a split second

00:00:41.122 --> 00:00:43.118
I've got 10 other tracks
that sound just like that.

00:00:43.118 --> 00:00:44.673
- [Angel] We do switch off.

00:00:44.673 --> 00:00:46.370
Usually every 30 minutes.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.224
She can kind of, like, move off of what I did.

00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:52.886
When we're not playing,
we're watching the audience.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:55.041
- She'll be playing and
I'll come over and whisper.

00:00:55.041 --> 00:00:56.867
I'll be like, play that next.

00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:59.732
- [Angel] I know when my
twin has it, we'll be okay.

00:00:59.732 --> 00:01:02.482
- [Dren] We grew up in the Bronx.

00:01:03.326 --> 00:01:05.011
- We grew up in the Bronx, New York.

00:01:05.011 --> 00:01:06.547
It's a really Jamaican area.

00:01:06.547 --> 00:01:09.737
A lot of reggae playing out
in the streets all the time.

00:01:09.737 --> 00:01:12.483
- [Dren] In fifth grade
we entered this program

00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:15.348
that helps inner-city youth

00:01:15.348 --> 00:01:17.631
that are generally under-privileged.

00:01:17.631 --> 00:01:20.871
- We got very lucky, but
some kids don't get as lucky.

00:01:20.871 --> 00:01:23.123
We got through middle
school and high school

00:01:23.123 --> 00:01:27.290
and we got into Dartmouth and
we both decided to go there.

00:01:28.313 --> 00:01:29.957
- To go.
- Hey guys.

00:01:29.957 --> 00:01:31.366
- Hey, hi.

00:01:31.366 --> 00:01:34.074
- So when we graduated, we
came back to the city.

00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:36.047
I was playing with equipment on and off.

00:01:36.047 --> 00:01:38.181
I went home one day and I told her

00:01:38.181 --> 00:01:40.278
like, this is what we have to do.

00:01:40.278 --> 00:01:42.292
After you graduate from college

00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:46.126
nobody's thinking you'll
then go on to become a DJ.

00:01:46.126 --> 00:01:47.991
It was one of those moments
where you had to be resolute

00:01:47.991 --> 00:01:50.660
in what you were doing.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.455
- [Dren] There's no kick yet.

00:01:52.455 --> 00:01:55.697
(hip-hop music)

00:01:55.697 --> 00:01:58.003
And then the bass hits.
- I kinda like it.

00:01:58.003 --> 00:02:00.047
- I think DJing is definitely

00:02:00.047 --> 00:02:03.011
a predominantly male industry.

00:02:03.011 --> 00:02:06.140
We've heard some negativity
from not even other DJs

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.263
but people in audiences.

00:02:08.263 --> 00:02:09.995
- And I think it's been
surprising just because

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:13.540
it doesn't feel like DJing
should be a gendered thing.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.132
I take a burden upon
myself to perform better

00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:18.185
because we are women.

00:02:18.185 --> 00:02:21.640
We do get a lot of good
feedback from girls and women.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.734
- Who want to learn to DJ.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.362
- Who want to learn how to DJ.

00:02:25.362 --> 00:02:27.572
- [Dren] If someone told
me that I would end up

00:02:27.572 --> 00:02:29.995
being a professional DJ with Angel

00:02:29.995 --> 00:02:31.832
I would not have believed it.

00:02:31.832 --> 00:02:35.816
- When you follow what you like
and you follow your dreams-

00:02:35.816 --> 00:02:38.066
- It can take you anywhere.

00:02:42.639 --> 00:02:44.556
(ding)

